        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'banner' conjures instant visual prominence and celebratory or promotional scale. Physically, it implies an eye-catching, durable display\u2014such as a vinyl roll-up banner welcoming delegates at an international trade convention or a grand-opening banner suspended across a retail storefront. Digitally, it denotes a horizontal top-of-page graphic ad designed to drive user clicks. Natives also instinctively understand the idiomatic adjective in 'a banner year' or 'banner quarter', signifying an extraordinary, record-breaking period of success.",
