        "evolution": "The term emerged in the late 19th and early 20th centuries alongside silent cinema and newsreel photography (c. 1900\u20131910) to designate professional motion-picture and still-camera technicians. Throughout the golden age of Hollywood and broadcast television, 'cameraman' was the universal industrial title. Since the late 20th century, gender-neutral industry alternatives such as 'camera operator' or 'cinematographer' have become standard in corporate and union credits, though 'cameraman' remains widely recognized in broadcast news and vernacular usage.",
