        "howNativesThink": "Native English speakers instinctively picture a technician behind a heavy broadcast camera on a tripod or a shoulder-mounted ENG rig, working in tandem with a reporter or director. While recognized as gendered (with modern corporate environments often adopting camera operator or videographer), cameraman remains the immediate colloquial and broadcast-news term for the visual technician in the field. Natives associate the word with quick reflexes, visual composition, and endurance in high-pressure media environments.",
