        "tips": "In TOEIC Part 7, reading passages often incorporate graphics, charts, and photographs with short italicized captions containing critical details (e.g., dates, names, source attributions). In Part 5, test-makers use false friends derived from the Latin root 'capere' (such as 'capture', 'captivity', or 'captor') to distract test-takers seeking the noun 'caption' (explanatory text under an image)."
