        "howNativesThink": "To native corporate executives and media professionals, 'crisis communication' represents the difference between organizational survival and catastrophic failure. Natives instinctively connect it with core ethical rules: never hide the truth, designate a single credible spokesperson, acknowledge harm with genuine empathy, present concrete mitigation steps immediately, and avoid speculative finger-pointing.",
