        "tips": "In TOEIC Part 5 and Part 7 texts (such as employee handbooks, manuals, and warranty documentation), the compound noun 'cross-reference' appears as the object of verbs like 'consult', 'verify', or 'include'. Be careful not to pick gerunds or participial adjectives when a standard countable compound noun is demanded after the definite article 'the'."
