        "commonMistakes": "Learners often place primary stress on the wrong syllable (*dis-SEM-i-na-tion* instead of *dis-sem-i-NA-tion*), or stumble over the double 's', mistakenly pronouncing it with a /z/ sound (*diz-zem-* rather than crisp /d\u026a\u02ccs\u025bm-/). Non-native speakers also sometimes confuse it with 'discrimination' or 'dissimulation' due to visual/orthographic similarity.",
