        "origin": "From Latin 'disseminationem' (nominative 'disseminatio', a scattering of seed), noun of action from the past-participle stem of 'disseminare' (to scatter seed, broadcast, spread abroad), composed of 'dis-' (in different directions, apart, abroad) and 'seminare' (to sow, plant seed), from 'semen' (seed, semen).",
