        "howNativesThink": "To a native English speaker, 'exclusive' operates on two distinct, powerful frequencies. In commercial communications and business law, it denotes monopoly or sole rights\u2014an 'exclusive contract' means no competitor can sell or distribute that asset. In media and public relations, an 'exclusive interview' or 'exclusive report' is a coveted journalistic triumph, meaning no other publication or network has access to the subject or story. Socially, it signals high-end prestige, catering exclusively to a vetted, elite clientele.",
