        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers immediately associate fidelity with two foundational concepts: strict accuracy to an original source (in technology, audio, video, and design) and unwavering steadfastness (in personal loyalty or corporate duty). When hearing 'high fidelity,' a native speaker visualizes crisp, studio-grade sound without hiss or distortion, or a digital app mockup that looks and functions like the real application. In communications, fidelity is the benchmark of technical perfection: it answers whether any meaning or acoustic quality was lost in transmission.",
