        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers envision a tangible, wall-mounted or desktop electronic console with a microphone grill, a push-to-talk button, and a built-in miniature speaker. The mental model is inherently localized and closed: an intercom connects Room A to Room B, the gate to the front desk, or the reception lobby to a specific tenant's office. Unlike a standard telephone call or email, an intercom transmission is instantaneous, often slightly acoustic or crackly, and used for brief, functional directives like 'Delivery driver at the service entrance' or 'Mr. Davies, your 2 o'clock visitor has arrived'.",
