        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a 'manuscript' represents creative work in progress before it becomes a finished 'book', 'article', or 'monograph'. It evokes stacks of typed pages with red-pen editorial annotations, double-spaced typography, margin notes, and query tracking. While historically it strictly meant handwritten parchment, modern publishing professionals use 'manuscript' (often abbreviated 'MS' or 'MSS') exclusively for the editable text version submitted by an author. When an editor asks 'Did you receive the manuscript?', they are asking for the full draft text ready for line editing.",
