        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers associate 'messaging' with two predominant domains: instant digital communications ('messaging app') and corporate message alignment ('brand messaging', 'on-message'). In business, marketing professionals view 'messaging' not merely as isolated text, but as a deliberate strategic discipline. It represents the curated talking points and value narratives that everyone from sales representatives to the chief executive must align with to prevent disjointed market perception.",
        "mentalImage": "A senior marketing strategist standing in front of a glass conference wall covered in color-coded cards mapping out customer pain points, value propositions, and core messaging pillars for an upcoming software release.",
