        "culturalContext": "In Anglo-American professional and public life, debates and industry symposiums rely heavily on the moderator's skill to maintain fair play and intellectual balance. In TOEIC listening and reading contexts, moderators frequently appear in Part 4 announcements, Part 3 conversations, and Part 7 event agendas, signaling transitions between speakers or introducing Q&A segments.",
        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, an effective 'moderator' is fundamentally neutral, diplomatic, and structured. A moderator does not inject personal biases, take sides, or dominate airtime; rather, their function is to elevate the panelists, ask incisive questions, ensure equal airtime, and politely cut off rambling speakers when time expires. In digital contexts, a moderator is viewed as the custodian of decorum who safeguards forum threads from abuse, spam, and off-topic detours.",
