        "culturalContext": "In English-speaking civic and business culture, independent news reporting is considered the bedrock of a free market and democratic society. TOEIC tests regularly feature news items in Part 4 (radio broadcasts covering traffic, weather, and business openings) and Part 7 (business newspaper articles and press releases reporting executive appointments and quarterly revenues).",
        "howNativesThink": "Native English speakers treat 'news' as fresh intelligence that alters someone's knowledge state. Unlike historical records or general data, 'news' implies immediate recency and personal or public relevance. Natives instinctively treat it as uncountable; they would never say 'I have two news for you', saying instead 'I have two pieces of news'. The proverb 'No news is good news' encapsulates how deeply the word is embedded in daily thought.",
