        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'on-air' conjures an immediate mental image of an illuminated bright red sign mounted above a soundproof studio door. It signals that nothing can be taken back: slips of the tongue, microphone thumps, or background coughs will immediately be broadcast to thousands or millions of listeners. In media careers, being 'on-air' distinguishes the visible/audible performers (the 'on-air personalities', anchors, correspondents) from behind-the-scenes producers, writers, and technical switchers. In corporate PR, securing an executive's 'on-air interview' is considered a high-stakes, high-reward media opportunity.",
        "mentalImage": "A television news anchor sitting behind a polished studio desk, looking directly into camera one with an earpiece, while an overhead red studio light box brightly glows 'ON AIR'.",
