        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a proofreader is the ultimate firewall against humiliating public mistakes. Native speakers sharply distinguish a proofreader from a writer or copyeditor: while an editor reshapes sentence rhythm and narrative flow, a proofreader exercises granular typographic vigilance\u2014catching double spaces, inverted quotation marks, incorrect folio numbers, and homophones. Having a proofreader inspect a document is seen as a hallmark of organizational professionalism and credibility.",
