        "howNativesThink": "To a native English speaker, 'publisher' carries institutional prestige and commercial weight. Natives strictly distinguish between the 'author' (the creative originator), the 'printer' (the manufacturing contractor), the 'editor' (the prose reviser), and the 'publisher' (the business entity that assumes legal and financial risk to bring the work into the public sphere). In corporate magazine and newspaper structures, 'the publisher' also denotes the senior corporate executive who leads business operations, advertising revenue, and publication strategy.",
