        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers understand \"reporting\" in two predominant professional frameworks: corporate compliance/governance and journalism. In corporate business, \"financial reporting\" or \"ESG reporting\" evokes systematic pipelines of data, accounting standards (GAAP/IFRS), and audited transparency that protect corporate integrity. Hierarchically, native speakers use \"reporting line\" to describe managerial reporting relationships. In journalism, \"investigative reporting\" signifies thorough fact-checking and ethical media coverage. Unlike a single \"report\", \"reporting\" conveys an ongoing operational discipline or standard.",
