        "commonMistakes": "A classic heteronym / stress-shift pitfall: learners frequently pronounce the noun with second-syllable stress (*re-PRINT*), which is the verb form, rather than initial stress (/\u02c8ri\u02d0pr\u026ant/). Learners also sometimes write it with an unnecessary hyphen (*re-print*) or confuse a \"reprint\" (an exact additional printing of identical existing text) with a \"new edition\" or \"revised edition\" (which contains rewritten chapters, updated figures, or substantial modifications).",
        "ipa": "/\u02c8ri\u02d0pr\u026ant/",
