        "tips": "In TOEIC Part 5, questions often evaluate whether test takers recognize the singular countable noun form following a singular indefinite article and an adjective (\"an urgent _____\"). (B) \"reprint\" is the correct singular noun. (A) is a past tense verb or past participle, (C) is an adjective, and (D) is a plural noun which cannot follow the singular article \"an\". Note also the stress distinction: the noun \"reprint\" is stressed on the first syllable (REE-print)."
