        "commonMistakes": "Learners frequently mispronounce the suffix '-sion' as voiceless /\u0283\u0259n/ (*re-VI-shun*) or /zi\u02d0.\u0259n/. The consonant is a voiced postalveolar fricative /\u0292/, yielding /r\u026a\u02c8v\u026a\u0292.\u0259n/. In addition, stress falls strictly on the second syllable, never the first (*REE-vi-sion*).",
