        "whenNotToUse": "Do not confuse with \"review\" (the evaluation or opinion itself) or \"reversal\" (completely overturning an earlier decision). Do not use \"revision\" when creating something entirely new from scratch.",
        "whenToUse": "Use when referring to concrete alterations, amendments, or updated drafts of documents, policies, schedules, blueprints, or contracts (e.g., \"make revisions to the draft\", \"subject to revision\", \"revision history\"). In Commonwealth English, use also for reviewing study notes before tests."
