        "tips": "The prepositional construction \"subject to revision\" is one of the most reliable recurring grammar patterns tested in TOEIC Part 5 and 6. The preposition \"to\" must be followed by a noun or noun phrase. Test writers frequently present verb forms like \"revise\", participles like \"revised\", or adverbs like \"revisingly\" to mislead candidates. Recognize \"revision\" as the required abstract noun."
