        "howNativesThink": "Native English speakers instinctively navigate two distinct yet conceptually linked realms for \"satellite\": 1) High-tech orbital telecommunications (satellite dishes, GPS navigation, satellite phones, live broadcast relays), and 2) A regional branch location that functions as an outpost of a primary central hub (a \"satellite office\" or \"satellite campus\"). The unifying intuition is always an auxiliary, communicative entity revolving around and dependent upon a primary central body.",
