        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers view a 'script' as an instrument of message control and risk mitigation, but also recognize the danger of sounding mechanical. To 'stick to the script' implies discipline and brand compliance\u2014crucial for legal briefings or product disclosures. In contrast, 'going off-script' suggests spontaneity, candor, or unvetted vulnerability. When evaluating customer service or telemarketing, native speakers readily distinguish between an agent who reads rigidly from a script and one who sounds conversational and empathetic while adhering to mandatory guidelines.",
