        "culturalContext": "In modern corporate life, a company's social media presence is just as critical as its website or public relations office. In the TOEIC, \"social media\" frequently appears in Part 7 reading passages (job descriptions for digital marketing coordinators, customer feedback notices, corporate strategy emails) and Part 3/4 business conversations discussing customer outreach and promotional campaigns.",
        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, \"social media\" refers collectively to the ecosystem of user-driven digital platforms (such as LinkedIn, X/Twitter, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok) where individuals and companies connect. In business, natives immediately think of audience engagement, brand perception, viral marketing, influencer partnerships, and online reputation management. Grammatically, native speakers overwhelmingly treat \"social media\" as an uncountable singular mass noun (\"Social media is changing...\") rather than plural, though academic contexts occasionally use plural verbs.",
