        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, 'storyboard' represents both a tangible creative artifact (a board or digital grid of illustrated scene panels) and the supreme symbol of thorough pre-production planning. In advertising and corporate media, you never spend budget on cameras, crews, or talent without an approved storyboard; it serves as the contract between the creative team and the paying client. In modern corporate parlance, it is also frequently used as a metaphor for plotting out user experience flows or structuring an executive presentation narrative step by step.",
