        "evolution": "Used for centuries in English to describe physical or poetic torrents of water, light, tears, or crowds. In the early 1990s, with the emergence of the World Wide Web and digital telecommunications, computer scientists adapted 'streaming' (such as 'streaming audio' and 'streaming video') to describe delivering data packets continuously over IP networks so that client devices could decode and play media immediately without downloading the entire file to local storage. By the 2000s and 2010s, high-speed fiber-optic and mobile broadband established streaming as the dominant global paradigm for consumer entertainment (e.g., Netflix, Spotify), enterprise webinars, video conferencing, and live corporate broadcasts.",
