    "nativeMindset": {
        "culturalContext": "In corporate governance, Anglo-American legal systems, and institutional business practices, formal submission processes ensure transparency, prevent favoritism, and establish an auditable record of receipt. In the TOEIC exam, 'submission' is among the highest-frequency testing words in Parts 5, 6, and 7, appearing in contexts like expense reimbursement policies, vendor bidding guidelines, job application deadlines, and contest rules.",
        "howNativesThink": "In commercial and professional environments, native speakers instinctively link 'submission' with deadlines, strict procedural requirements, and formal evaluation. A submission is not just casually handing something over; it implies entering a formal process where your work will be vetted against specific criteria (RFPs, grant guidelines, contest rules, job requirements). Natives also understand the dual meaning: 'the submission of the report' (the procedural action) versus 'we received forty submissions' (the physical or digital proposals themselves). Late submission is universally understood to mean automatic disqualification.",
        "mentalImage": "A sleek corporate conference room where three neatly bound, official tender dossiers stamped 'CONFIDENTIAL BID SUBMISSION' rest on a polished mahogany table alongside a laptop showing a submission confirmation timestamp.",
        "whenNotToUse": "Do not confuse with 'admission' (conceding a mistake, or gaining entry into an institution or event), 'permission' (formal consent or authorization to act), or 'transmission' (the electronic or mechanical sending of signals, data, or power). Avoid using 'submission' for informal handoffs, such as passing a memo to a coworker.",
        "whenToUse": "Use when referring to the formal delivery or presenting of proposals, bids, job applications, contest entries, insurance claims, expense reports, or scholarly manuscripts for official evaluation (e.g., 'submission deadline', 'tender submission', 'online submission portal', 'formal submission of documents')."
    },
