        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers immediately associate 'telemarketing' with unsolicited cold calls, telemarketing call centers, and dinner-time sales pitches. In a corporate business environment, however, it is viewed as an inside-sales outreach discipline focused on pipeline generation, lead qualification, and setting appointments for field account executives.",
        "mentalImage": "A bustling corporate contact center where rows of outbound sales development representatives wear noise-canceling headsets with boom microphones, scanning dynamic call scripts on computer monitors while auto-dialers populate the next phone record.",
        "whenNotToUse": "Do not use for customer service or technical support hotlines (use 'customer care', 'help desk', or 'technical support'). Do not use for email marketing ('email campaigns'), web advertising ('digital advertising' or 'PPC'), or face-to-face door-to-door selling ('canvassing' or 'direct sales').",
        "whenToUse": "Use when referring to phone-based promotional campaigns, outbound cold-calling drives, lead generation operations, or outsourced call center sales services (e.g., 'The retail bank expanded its telemarketing division to introduce mortgage refinancing options to existing depositors')."
