        "evolution": "Originally invented in 1950 by Fred Barton Jr., Hubert Schlafly, and Irving Berlin Kahn and trademarked as 'TelePrompTer' by the TelePrompTer Corporation, the initial system used a motorized mechanical roll of butcher paper behind television cameras. By the 1980s, it evolved into electronic CRT and flat-panel displays reflecting scrolling text onto specialized beam-splitter glass. The trademark subsequently genericized into the common noun 'teleprompter'.",
