        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers view a 'transmitter' as the physical origin point in a two-part communication link: the 'transmitter and receiver' pair (often integrated as a 'transceiver'). Instinctively, native speakers associate 'transmitter' with hardware\u2014such as broadcast radio towers, handheld walkie-talkies, wireless clip-on microphones, garage remotes, or telemetry sensors in logistics and manufacturing. It conveys tangible engineering, signal propagation, and wireless connectivity.",
