        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a 'voiceover' (often written as 'voiceover' or 'voice-over') immediately conjures the invisible narrator guiding the listener through a documentary, a charismatic voice introducing a new luxury car on a TV commercial, or an instructional voice walking through a software demo. In business and corporate communications, native speakers associate voiceovers with professional polish\u2014hiring a professional voiceover artist is what separates a low-budget, amateur promotional clip from a high-stakes, broadcast-ready corporate video.",
