        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers use 'airwaves' both technically (referencing the licensed electromagnetic spectrum) and idiomatically (referencing radio and TV programming). Phrases like 'hit the airwaves' mean a broadcast advertisement or show is airing publicly. Culturally, native speakers associate 'the airwaves' with a public good: historically, governments license airwave frequencies on the condition that broadcasters serve the public interest and adhere to decency guidelines.",
