        "howNativesThink": "In corporate communications, marketing, and publishing, native speakers immediately associate \"character\" with strict technical constraints\u2014specifically character limits and counts for SEO meta titles, SMS broadcasts, ad headlines, and push notifications. Unlike the word \"letter\", a native speaker instinctively knows that a \"character\" encompasses spaces, hyphens, and punctuation marks. In media and scriptwriting, they readily differentiate the live actor from the fictional \"character\" portrayed.",
