        "howNativesThink": "In corporate communications, advertising, and entertainment media, native speakers recognize a 'composer' not merely as a classical musician, but as an essential commercial partner who shapes brand identity through sound. A commercial composer crafts the emotional architecture of a commercial, podcast, or corporate documentary, translating abstract marketing values (such as trust, exhilaration, or reliability) into melodic motifs and sonic signatures. Native executives also think of composers in terms of copyright, performance royalties (ASCAP, BMI), and work-for-hire agreements.",
